A||||14||Carrolles||Check out Large Capacity Hand Riveter at harbor Freight||||1||
Z||000000||Carrolles||01-24-2000||09:03 AM||||I ordered ths Large Capacity Hand Riveter from Harbor Freight and am anxious to get it.  It should handle the power window/pdl rivets.  Comes with nosepieces for 1/8", 3/16", 3/32", and 1/4" diameter rivets and includes 25 of each size rivet.<P>Go to <A HREF="http://www.harborfreight.com" TARGET=_blank>www.harborfreight.com</A> <BR>and look up item number 41291<P>$16.99||||reg||1
Z||000001||pherder||01-24-2000||12:45 PM||||I have been waiting over a month for mine.<P>They have them back ordered.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Paul||||reg||8
Z||000002||Carrolles||01-24-2000||01:10 PM||||I called customer service and they said mine is due to ship today and to expect to see it in 10 to 14 business days.  I originally ordered it on 12/22/99.<BR>I'm also waiting for my blast cabinet which was supposed to have shipped on 1/13/00.  Should see it in a week or two.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfixit58||01-24-2000||02:01 PM||||Hey Carrollas,<P>If you ordered the bench-top bead blaster be aware that before you use it, be sure to caulk all the seams, especially the bottom. I got one last year and didn't caulk anything and before long, my garage was a mess and there were glass beads all over the work area. <P>You probably want to take a dryer hose from the air vent in the back and run it outside to keep the dust down. Also,the air trigger on my blaster handle went bad rather quickly. I just turn mine on and off with the air valve. <P>But, it's a great tool for less than $100,<BR>Roy L.||||reg||4
Z||000004||David Gamache||01-24-2000||06:25 PM||||I was thinking about picking up one of these ,but was not sure where to get one. Thanks for the info. Does anyone know of a place that sells a plastic rivet gun for a better price than NAPA (27.99$). I have not checked harbor yet, but I will.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carrolles||01-25-2000||07:01 AM||||I believe the Harbor Freight Large Capacity Riveter will also do the plastic rivets.||||reg||1
Z||000006||WKDFIRO||01-25-2000||04:13 PM||||Harbor Freight is sooo cool! I love just walking around and looking at all of the cool stuff in their stores.||||reg||6
Z||000007||RossT||06-27-2000||04:49 AM||||I was just curious, "carrolles" did your riveter ever come in? and if so how did it work on your side windows?  What type of rivet did you end up using plastic/metal and size??  I need to do my side window.  The local autoglass place wants $210.  But I can by the glass for $88  at my local auto parts store. Has anyone else done the side window? How did you re-attach the glass once you drilled out the rivets.<P>Thanks...||||reg||1
Z||000008||Carrolles||06-27-2000||07:18 AM||||Yes, the riveter came in.  It is very sturdy and comes with nose pieces for 1/16", 1/8", 3/16", and 1/4" rivets.  It also included 25 of each size rivet in steel.<P>The rivets are exactly like those that hold the window and lock mechanisms in the door.  I'm finally in the process of upgrading to power windows and locks.  I'm stripping the mechanism out of a pair of donor doors I got at Ed Park's swap meet ($45 for two doors, not bad).  I pulled the wiring harness out of a donor from a salvage yard ($15).<P>I'd recommend the Hand Riveter.  While I was waiting on delivery of mine Harbor Freight lowered the price to $12.99.  Oh well, $16.99 still is a great price.<P>Take care,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000009||fiero56||06-27-2000||08:58 AM||||Hey Ross, I will GIVE you a passenger side window free of charge except for shipping if you want it. It is in very good condition(no scratches, etc). Let me know if you want it.||||reg||1
Z||000010||bHooper||06-27-2000||09:39 AM||||do you think this riveter can pull those rivets that attach the body panels to the car?<P>i think they are 3/8" alumminum.  <P>thanks,<BR>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000011||TOM||06-27-2000||10:51 AM||||All the power window conversions I have done I have used nuts and bolts. They work just fine and I have a big riveter.||||reg||1
Z||000012||RossT||06-27-2000||11:49 PM||||Fiero56, Thanks for the offer, but it is actually the drivers side door glass that i need. That is a great offer "free" Thanks again.<P>Carrolles, Thanks for the update.  I may go ahead and order it.<P>Tom, What size nut and bolts are you using? are they plastic or metal. Do they every come loose, or do you use locktight..<P>Thanks again for the update!!<P>Ross||||reg||1
Z||000013||fiero56||06-28-2000||07:48 AM||||I also have a good drivers side door glass sitting here too, if you want it. Just say the word and its on its way.||||reg||1
